WEBVTT

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:31.416
but for some reason
I haven't opened this box.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.776
And I felt like there was
a key to this, somehow,

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:37.176
in talking about something at TED
that I haven't discussed before,

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.416
and bored people elsewhere.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:41.696
So I thought, maybe
there's something with this.

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:43.616
And there was this giant question mark.

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:46.176
I love the design,
for what it's worth, of this thing.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.456
And I started thinking,
why haven't I opened it?

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.376
And I realized that I haven't opened it

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.976
because it represents
something important -- to me.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.400
It represents my grandfather.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:56.736
Am I allowed to cry at TED?

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:58.475
Because -- no, I'm not going to cry.

00:04:58.499 --> 00:04:59.656
(Laughter)

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:00.831
But --